Feature: Data Standardization of Delivery Date

  Background: Prepare the environment
    Given a SQL file located at /Workspace/stg/scripts/f_order.sql
    And using Unity Catalog purgo_databricks with Schema purgo_playground

  Scenario: Verify if delivery_dt is in Decimal (38,0) format with yyyymmdd
    Given the table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_order
    When the delivery_dt field is extracted
    Then the delivery_dt should be in Decimal (38,0) format
    And the values should match the pattern yyyymmdd

  Scenario Outline: Check invalid delivery_dt formats
    Given the delivery_dt value "<delivery_dt_value>"
    When converted to the target format
    Then an error message "<error_message>" should be returned

    Examples:
      | delivery_dt_value | error_message                     |
      | 2024-09-10        | "Invalid format: should be yyyymmdd" |
      | 2024/09/10        | "Invalid format: should be yyyymmdd" |
      | 20240910.5        | "Invalid decimal format"           |

  Scenario: Validate conversion error conditions
    Given the delivery_dt value is not in "yyyymmdd" format
    When the conversion logic is applied
    Then log an error "Conversion failed: Invalid source format"

  Scenario: Validate correct values
    Given the delivery_dt in table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_order
    When queried for all entries
    Then each delivery_dt should pass the format conversion

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven tests for different delivery_dt inputs
    Given the delivery_dt is "<input_value>"
    When processed in the conversion pipeline
    Then the resultant format should be "<expected_output>"

    Examples:
      | input_value | expected_output |
      | 20240910    | 20240910        |
      | 20231201    | 20231201        |
      | 20230115    | 20230115        |
